## Worked example
Given a diff adding a public method to a service, a good generated test looks like:

```java
package com.example;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;

public class PriceServiceTest {

    @Test
    void appliesDiscount() {
        PriceService service = new PriceService();
        assertEquals(90, service.withDiscount(100, 0.1));
    }
}
```

Note the test class naming (ends with `Test`), the required annotations, and the direct assertion
on the changed behavior. Emulate this style for every changed class.

